4. LIMITED PRACTICAL VALUE OF CLONING

---

The repository is intentionally not a turnkey copy of the live business. A
clone of this repository will not function as a finished product for you,
because:

(a) Private and environment-specific files are excluded, including .env
files, API keys, Firebase and database credentials, service accounts
and the administrator configuration.
(b) Image and brand assets are not included in the repository.
(c) The Project depends on accounts and services owned by the Main Author
(including the Groq API key, the Firebase project, the Firestore
security rules and the administrator UID list). None of these are
shared and you would need to create your own.
(d) All branding, text, team data, projects, pricing and contact details
belong to the Main Author and describe his business. You would have to
replace every one of them, at which point you would be building your
own project rather than using this one.
(e) Using the Project as-is, or with only superficial modifications, would
violate Section 3 of this license.

In summary, a clone requires substantial changes in order to work, and you are
not permitted to use the Project for your own purposes in any case.

